# Offline priority (hard)

This project stays **offline-first**. Local ChatRouter / Ollama / on-machine tools are the product path.

## Do

- Prefer localhost backends (`127.0.0.1`, Ollama, ChatRouter, local Ghidra MCP).
- Design vision, OCR, captioning, and coding so they work with **no cloud API calls**.
- If hardware cannot run a capability yet, document it as an **open problem to solve** (VRAM, model size, latency). Do not “fix” it by escalating to Gemini / Claude / Cursor cloud / any internet LLM.

## Opt-in web research (not cloud escalate)

- `blossom.web.enabled` (default **true**) exposes `web_search` / `fetch_url` / `browser_*`. Blossom chooses those tools at its own volition (need-based) — users should not need to say “search the web.” Set to false for a fully offline workspace.
- That path is **distinct** from cloud LLM escalate (`ESCALATE_GEMINI` / Claude / Cursor) and from vision `onAttach=escalate`.
- Never silently call the public internet when web is off. Cloud LLM/vision escalate remains non-default.

## Do not

- Add or recommend internet escalations as the default for screenshots, OCR, coding, or “when stuck.”
- Treat cloud vision (Gemini/Claude/Cursor Agent online) as the solution path for this repo’s product behavior.
- Silently widen `blossom.vision.onAttach` / escalate chains toward the public internet without an explicit user override for a one-off experiment.
- Collapse “need docs” into cloud LLM handoff when opt-in web tools are available.

## When blocked by hardware

State the gap plainly, e.g.:

- “Local VL model needs ≥N GB VRAM; machine has M — problem to solve.”
- “OCR quality on dark UI toasts is poor without preprocess — problem to solve.”

Then propose **local** mitigations (smaller VL model, CPU OCR + preprocess, caption cache, crop-to-toast, etc.). Never substitute cloud.
